Now, the `isSyntheticUserText` predicate — settle notices are synthetic user text (for the obligations ledger). Fine.

Let me now also decide the exact marker format for the label. Ticket: "keep id, state, exit code, first/last ~120 chars of the command". I'll do:

```dart
const shellJobLabelHeadChars = 120;
const shellJobLabelTailChars = 120;

String shellJobCommandLabel(
  String command, {
  int headChars = shellJobLabelHeadChars,
  int tailChars = shellJobLabelTailChars,
}) {
  final flat = command.replaceAll(RegExp(r'\s+'), ').trim();
  final budget = headChars + tailChars;
  if (flat.length <= budget) return flat;
  final head = _codepointSafeSlice(flat, 0, headChars);
  final tail = _codepointSafeSlice(flat, flat.length - tailChars, flat.length);
  final omitted = flat.length - head.length - tail.length;
  return '$head […$omitted chars…] $tail';
}
```

Codepoint-safe cut (surrogate pairs) — copy the `_headExcerpt`/`_tailExcerpt` approach from spill.dart. Actually — can I reuse those? They're private in spill.dart. Small duplication is fine but better: put a public helper somewhere shared. `lib/src/utils/`? Let me check what's in utils.

