Interesting! My test found a real edge in the EXISTING `buildPreview`: when `headChars + tailChars >= body.length`, `omitted` goes NEGATIVE (`-1500`!). My body is 1500 chars with head/tail bounds of 2000 each → head = whole body, tail = whole body, omitted = 1500 - 1500 - 1500 = -1500. So buildPreview prints `[... -1500 chars omitted ...]` and DOUBLES the whole body (head + tail). That's a pre-existing bug in spill.dart: threshold 1000 < head+tail bounds 4000 → a spilled body smaller than the preview bounds renders TWICE plus a negative omitted count.

This is exactly the kind of thing a bench cap at a small threshold would hit! A bench run setting FAH_SPILL_THRESHOLD=8192 is fine (8192 > 4000), but a threshold BELOW 4000 chars triggers the bug. My test used threshold 1000 with a 1500-char body → boom.

Fix `buildPreview` (or `_headExcerpt`/`_tailExcerpt` interplay): when head + tail cover the body, render the body once with no omitted marker. The cleanest fix in `buildPreview`:

```dart
final head = _headExcerpt(body, config.headChars);
final tail = _tailExcerpt(body, config.tailChars);
final omitted = body.length - head.length - tail.length;
if (omitted <= 0) {
  // The preview bounds cover the whole body: render it once, no marker.
  return header + body + readHint;
}
```

Wait, but head and tail might overlap/interleave weirdly (head is first X, tail last Y; if X+Y ≥ len they jointly cover the body but the concatenation head+tail = body exactly when they don't overlap mid-string... e.g. body len 1500, head 2000 = whole body; tail 2000 = whole body → head+tail = 2×body. The single-render fix returns the body once. If head < body and head+tail ≥ len (e.g. len 3000, head 2000, tail 2000 → head = first 2000, tail = last 2000, overlap = 1000; concat = 4000 chars ≠ body). So when omitted ≤ 0, the right render = the whole body once (both bounds cover it). Implement that.

This is a genuine pre-existing bug fix — in scope (my ticket needs small thresholds to work). Fix buildPreview in spill.dart.

