Wait — but the OLD code passed the PTY test with `shellJobCommandPreview` = FIRST LINE ONLY + '…'. So the owner's actual invariant: THE SETTLE NOTICE CARRIES THE FIRST LINE ONLY. The ticket asks for first/last ~120 of the command. These CONFLICT for multi-line commands. The owner frame (issue #599) is the stronger, pre-existing contract — 'the body is never a transcript row source'. The ticket's 'first/last ~120 chars' targets the BENCH evidence: multi-KB SINGLE-LINE pipelines (where first/last 120 of the line is right).

