SIMPLER, OWNER-FAITHFUL RULE: for multi-line commands, the label keeps the FIRST LINE (bounded to headChars) and appends '…N chars omitted…' — no tail. For single-line commands (the bench evidence class), first/last 120. Rationale: for a multi-line command the "tail action" claim is unsafe (the tail may be body), and the first line IS the command's face. The ticket's tail value ('; make test') lives in the single-line class ✓.

